          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Dissolution of $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4$ in water is an exothermic process. When a substance dissolves in water by an exothermic process, its solubility decreases with an increase in temperature. Hence, solubility of $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4$ in water decreases with increase in temperature.",
